{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Rephidim.</b> What is the reason to go back and state from where they journeyed — has Scripture not already written that they were encamping at Rephidim, so is it not known that they journeyed from there? Rather, to juxtapose their journeying from Rephidim to their arrival at the wilderness of Sinai: just as their arrival at the wilderness of Sinai was in repentance, so their journeying from Rephidim was in repentance (Mekhilta)." "<b>And Israel encamped there.</b> As one man with one heart — but all the other encampments were in murmuring and in strife." "<b>Opposite the mountain.</b> To its east. And everywhere you find נֶגֶד, it means facing east (ibid.)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:04.055000102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}